      "text": "1. this is more of an ansi terminal formatter\nwhich includes things like colorizing, some text\nediting like italics and so on. Only for terminal\nformatting",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. this is more of an ansi terminal formatter which includes things like colorizing, some text editing like italics and so on. Only for terminal formatting",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pTeSpaIzlz7shiFS8MG18",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6267.8061496753235,
      "y": 22.222901917909326,
      "width": 391.24399966417445,
      "height": 273.9049010086242,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "twluPLBX9Ta0jwjlF3if0",
      "index": "b2a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 368684224,
      "version": 3741,
      "versionNonce": 1693986624,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763109961715,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Represents the storage interface for storing\ndata relevant to paxos protocol\n\n   a) node state as a state to persist\n \n   b) consensus value as a state to persist\n      - we can just keep a log of these values\nand load its head and so on\n\n2. abstracts out all the persistence lifecycle\nfunctionality e.g. snapshotting of node state,\nloading of snapshotted value, committing to\nthe local record log (local to node)",
      "fontSize": 16.855686215915338,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Represents the storage interface for storing data relevant to paxos protocol\n\n   a) node state as a state to persist\n \n   b) consensus value as a state to persist\n      - we can just keep a log of these values and load its head and so on\n\n2. abstracts out all the persistence lifecycle functionality e.g. snapshotting of node state, loading of snapshotted value, committing to the local record log (local to node)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
