    {
      "id": "EwR-DRFEiC-5_CbKrnXR-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7195.254842244721,
      "y": -59.73870883666871,
      "width": 474.6333312988281,
      "height": 460,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "twluPLBX9Ta0jwjlF3if0",
      "index": "b2o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 322125632,
      "version": 5879,
      "versionNonce": 1303541804,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763210953742,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "[DECISION] \n\nthe initial intent for passing storage module into the Make\nnode functor was so that we can do a swapping of different\ntypes of storage. \n\nCurrently the problem we're facing is a messy dependency\ntree when it comes to us actually using the storage.\n\nThis happens because we want to store the following\nthings: \n  1. node state \n  2. consensus related info\n\nto store 1, node_state must exist prior to the existence of\nstorage so that we can use it. This approach will work but\nit would mean that we need to pass Node_state in as a\nparameter. This feels a little messy. \n\nFor now, we shall choose to keep storage within node itself\nso that we won't have this mess. Now, Make_node can be\ncalled by simulator, which instantiates the node module (and\nalso its storage), avoiding a bunch of dependency issues.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "22EfsCxZ4WmvCXjP4BKN-",
      "originalText": "[DECISION] \n\nthe initial intent for passing storage module into the Make node functor was so that we can do a swapping of different types of storage. \n\nCurrently the problem we're facing is a messy dependency tree when it comes to us actually using the storage.\n\nThis happens because we want to store the following things: \n  1. node state \n  2. consensus related info\n\nto store 1, node_state must exist prior to the existence of storage so that we can use it. This approach will work but it would mean that we need to pass Node_state in as a parameter. This feels a little messy. \n\nFor now, we shall choose to keep storage within node itself so that we won't have this mess. Now, Make_node can be called by simulator, which instantiates the node module (and also its storage), avoiding a bunch of dependency issues.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rzXztGuJuYqGfrAwPH0e5",
