    {
      "id": "JBH0VMMLXYQP2918znV6B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4876.653338823556,
      "y": 835.9146048695864,
      "width": 431.4222757596183,
      "height": 484.60097870756596,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "twluPLBX9Ta0jwjlF3if0",
      "index": "b37",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1782885036,
      "version": 4254,
      "versionNonce": 1580129068,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763383888242,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "[purpose]\n1. Stateless, passive event_bus that offers a\ncommunication channel that is topic-driven and\ncarries messages. Is polymorphic in the callback type\nto allow us to define any callbacks. \n   - it's typically just V.t Message.t which is the\nconcretised version of this payload (i.e. the\nmessage containing the Value payload) is what the\nevent bus uses. \n\n2. It is also buffered so as to serve as a precursor\nto async event-simulations. Buffer is accumulated\nvia enqueing messages to it and drained @ every\ntick of the simulation\n\n3. Supports communication API via message-passing:\n  - broadcasting / unicasting to subscribers (just\nnodes for now) \n\n4. handles lifecycle of subscriptions (subscribe,\nunsubscribe)\n\n5. keeps track of some basic stats (mutable state)",
      "fontSize": 16.855686215915338,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "[purpose]\n1. Stateless, passive event_bus that offers a communication channel that is topic-driven and carries messages. Is polymorphic in the callback type to allow us to define any callbacks. \n   - it's typically just V.t Message.t which is the concretised version of this payload (i.e. the message containing the Value payload) is what the event bus uses. \n\n2. It is also buffered so as to serve as a precursor to async event-simulations. Buffer is accumulated via enqueing messages to it and drained @ every tick of the simulation\n\n3. Supports communication API via message-passing: \n  - broadcasting / unicasting to subscribers (just nodes for now) \n\n4. handles lifecycle of subscriptions (subscribe, unsubscribe)\n\n5. keeps track of some basic stats (mutable state)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
